const e={id:"gs-node-git-setup",title:{en:"Node.js, npm & Git Installation",hi:"Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide"},difficulty:"Beginner",readTime:9,sections:[{id:"concept",type:"concept",heading:{en:"Core Runtimes & Version Control Foundations",hi:"Node.js, npm Aur Git Ka Foundation"},body:{en:`Before building full-stack applications, your machine requires three fundamental software engines:

1. **Node.js (LTS Version)**:
   Always install the **LTS (Long Term Support)** version of Node.js. LTS releases are thoroughly battle-tested for enterprise production stability, whereas "Current" releases contain experimental features that may break packages.
2. **npm (Node Package Manager)**:
   Installed automatically alongside Node.js. npm allows you to install, update, and manage open-source JavaScript libraries (Express, React, Mongoose) from the central registry.
3. **Git (Distributed Version Control System)**:
   Git tracks every line change in your code over time, allows you to create experimental branches, and collaborate with team members across the globe via GitHub.`,hi:`Full-stack apps banane se pehle aapke computer mein teen foundational software engines hona zaroori hain:

1. **Node.js (LTS Version)**:
   Hamesha **LTS (Long Term Support)** version hi download karein. LTS version enterprise production ke liye stable hota hai. "Current" version mein naye experiments hote hain jo packages ko tod sakte hain.
2. **npm (Node Package Manager)**:
   Node install karte hi npm sath mein automatically install ho jata hai. Iske zariye aap hazaron libraries (jaise Express, React) ek command se install karte hain.
3. **Git (Version Control System)**:
   Git aapke code ka complete history track karta hai. Agar kal aapka code kharab ho jaye, toh aap ek second mein purane sahi code par wapas ja sakte hain.`},code:{language:"bash",filename:"verify-installation.sh",snippet:`# Verify your Node.js version (Recommended: v18+ or v20+)
node -v

# Verify npm version (Recommended: 9+)
npm -v

# Verify Git version
git --version`}},{id:"why-it-matters",type:"concept",heading:{en:"Why Version Control is Non-Negotiable",hi:"Git Aur Version Control Kyun Compulsory Hai?"},body:{en:`Without Git, developers resort to terrible folder naming like:
- \`project_final\`
- \`project_final_v2\`
- \`project_final_really_working\`

One accidental delete or computer crash wipes out weeks of hard work.

**With Git:**
- Every milestone is permanently saved with a cryptographic hash.
- You can experiment freely on a new branch without risking working code.
- You can host your projects publicly on GitHub to showcase to recruiters.`,hi:`Bina Git ke developers aisi ajeeb files banate hain:
- \`project_final\`
- \`project_final_final_v2\`
- \`project_ab_pakka_chalega\`

Agar system kharab ho jaye ya file delete ho jaye, toh hafton ki mehnat khatam.

**Git ke sath:**
- Har commit ek permanent save checkpoint ban jata hai.
- Aap nayi branch banakar bina dare naye features test kar sakte hain.
- Aapka code GitHub cloud par safe rehta hai aur companies ko dikhane ke kaam aata hai.`}},{id:"analogy",type:"analogy",heading:{en:"The Video Game Save Point Analogy",hi:"Video Game Ke Checkpoint Aur Save File Ka Udaharan"},body:{en:"Think of Git like the save points in an adventure video game:\n\n- **Working Directory**: You are playing the level, collecting coins, and trying tricky jumps.\n- **`git add` (The Staging Area)**: You reach a safe platform and stand near the glowing save stone. You prepare to record your progress.\n- **`git commit` (The Checkpoint Save)**: You press the save button. The game writes your exact health, inventory, and location to the memory card with a timestamp. If a boss defeats you later, you immediately respawn at this exact moment!\n- **`git push` (Cloud Backup)**: Syncing your local memory card saves to PlayStation Network or Xbox Cloud so you can play on any console in the world.",hi:"Git ko ek **Video Game ke Save Point** ki tarah samjhein:\n\n- **Working Directory**: Aap game khel rahe hain, coins collect kar rahe hain.\n- **`git add` (Staging Area)**: Aap ek safe platform par checkpoint ke samne khade ho gaye hain.\n- **`git commit` (Save Button Dabana)**: Aapne save daba diya! Ab game memory card mein aapka health, coins aur time save ho chuka hai. Agar aage chalkar game crash bhi ho jaye, toh aap wapas isi checkpoint se shuru kar sakte hain!\n- **`git push` (Cloud Sync)**: Local memory card ke save file ko PlayStation/Xbox Cloud par upload karna taaki computer kharab hone par bhi data safe rahe."}},{id:"syntax",type:"syntax",heading:{en:"The Essential Git Command Flow",hi:"Git Ka Essential Command Flow"},body:{en:'### The 4-Step Everyday Git Workflow\n\n1. **Check Status**: `git status` (See what files you added or modified).\n2. **Stage Changes**: `git add .` (Stage all modified files for commit).\n3. **Commit with Message**: `git commit -m "feat: setup express server"` (Record the snapshot).\n4. **Push to Remote**: `git push origin main` (Upload to GitHub).\n\n---\n\n### The Power of .gitignore\nNever push temporary, heavy, or sensitive files to GitHub:\n- `node_modules/`: Gigabytes of downloaded dependencies. Anyone can recreate it with `npm install`.\n- `.env`: Secret passwords and database credentials.',hi:'### Rozana Ka 4-Step Git Workflow\n\n1. **Status Check**: `git status` (Dekhein kaunsi files badli hain).\n2. **Staging**: `git add .` (Files ko save hone ke liye tayyar karein).\n3. **Commit**: `git commit -m "feat: user login api banayi"` (Checkpoint save karein).\n4. **Push**: `git push origin main` (GitHub cloud par upload karein).\n\n---\n\n### .gitignore Ka Rule\nYeh files kabhi bhi GitHub par push NA karein:\n- `node_modules/`: Hazaron heavy downloaded files. Kisi ko zaroorat ho toh wo `npm install` chala sakta hai.\n- `.env`: Secret database passwords aur private keys.'}},{id:"examples",type:"example",heading:{en:"Example 1 (Basic): Creating a Production .gitignore",hi:"Example 1 (Basic): Production .gitignore File Banana"},body:{en:"Always create a `.gitignore` file at the very root of your repository before making your first commit:",hi:"Pehle commit se pehle project ke root folder mein `.gitignore` zaroor banayein:"},code:{language:"bash",filename:".gitignore",snippet:`# Dependencies (Never commit!)
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js

# Environment Variables & Secrets (CRITICAL)
.env
.env.local
.env.production

# Build Output
dist/
build/

# Operating System Files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*`}},{id:"example-intermediate",type:"example",heading:{en:"Example 2 (Intermediate): Initializing & Linking a New GitHub Repo",hi:"Example 2 (Intermediate): Local Folder Ko GitHub Se Connect Karna"},body:{en:"The exact commands to turn a local directory into a Git repository and push it to GitHub for the first time:",hi:"Apne computer ke folder ko GitHub par first time live karne ke commands:"},code:{language:"bash",filename:"first-git-push.sh",snippet:`# 1. Initialize local repository
git init

# 2. Configure your identity (once per computer)
git config --global user.name "Aman Verma"
git config --global user.email "aman@example.com"

# 3. Stage and commit
git add .
git commit -m "chore: initial commit with project scaffold"

# 4. Rename default branch to main
git branch -M main

# 5. Link to your GitHub remote repository
git remote add origin https://github.com/your-username/mern-learning-hub.git

# 6. Push local commits to GitHub
git push -u origin main`}},{id:"example-real-world",type:"example",heading:{en:"Example 3 (Real-World): Feature Branching Workflow",hi:"Example 3 (Real-World): Industry Feature Branching Pattern"},body:{en:"Professional software companies never push directly to `main`. Engineers work on feature branches and create Pull Requests (PRs):",hi:"Professional tech companies mein direct `main` branch par code nahi daala jata. Feature branch banakar PR create ki jaati hai:"},code:{language:"bash",filename:"feature-branch-workflow.sh",snippet:`# 1. Pull latest changes from team
git checkout main
git pull origin main

# 2. Create and switch to an isolated feature branch
git checkout -b feature/jwt-authentication

# 3. Work, test, and commit changes
git add src/middleware/auth.js
git commit -m "feat(auth): implement jwt token verification middleware"

# 4. Push feature branch to GitHub
git push origin feature/jwt-authentication

# 5. On GitHub: Open Pull Request (PR) -> Team Reviews -> Merge to main!`}},{id:"mistakes",type:"mistakes",heading:{en:"Catastrophic Git Mistakes to Avoid",hi:"Git Ke Bada Nuksan Karwane Wale Mistakes"},body:{en:"### 1. Accidentally Committing 'node_modules/'\n- **The Disaster**: You stage 40,000 files taking 500 MB. GitHub rejects the push with: `File exceeds 100.00 MB limit`.\n- **The Fix**: Add `node_modules/` to `.gitignore`. Then run:\n```bash\ngit rm -r --cached node_modules\ngit commit -m \"chore: untrack node_modules\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Pushing Your Database Password or Stripe Secret Key to Public GitHub\n- **The Disaster**: Bots continuously scan GitHub public commits. Within 30 seconds of pushing a key, bots can hijack your database or AWS account!\n- **The Fix**: Put secrets in `.env`. If you accidentally committed it, immediately rotate (invalidate) the key in MongoDB Atlas or Stripe console.",hi:"### 1. 'node_modules' Ko Commit Kar Dena\n- **Problem**: 40,000 files stage ho jaati hain aur GitHub push reject kar deta hai: `File exceeds 100 MB`.\n- **Solution**: `.gitignore` mein `node_modules/` likhein aur yeh command chalayein:\n```bash\ngit rm -r --cached node_modules\ngit commit -m \"chore: remove node_modules from git\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Database Password Ya Secret Keys GitHub Par Push Karna\n- **Problem**: Internet par automated bots hote hain jo GitHub par secret keys dhundte hain aur cloud accounts hack kar lete hain.\n- **Solution**: Hamesha secrets ko `.env` mein rakhein. Agar galti se push ho jaye, toh turant MongoDB Atlas console mein jaakar naya password generate karein."}},{id:"best-practices",type:"summary",heading:{en:"Git & Node Best Practices",hi:"Git & Node Best Practices"},body:{en:"- Commit small changes frequently with descriptive messages.\n- Never commit `.env` or API keys.\n- Always install Node LTS.\n- Run `git status` before every `git add` to verify what changed.",hi:"- Chote-chote commits karein taaki rollback karna aasan ho.\n- `.env` file ko hamesha `.gitignore` mein daalein.\n- Hamesha Node.js ka LTS version install karein.\n- Commit karne se pehle hamesha `git status` check karein."}},{id:"interview",type:"interview",heading:{en:"Git & Package Management Interview Questions",hi:"Git & npm Interview Questions"},body:{en:"Standard questions asked in screening rounds:",hi:"Screening rounds ke standard questions:"},questions:[{q:{en:"What is the difference between package.json and package-lock.json?",hi:"package.json aur package-lock.json mein kya farq hota hai?"},a:{en:"package.json specifies the approximate dependencies and version ranges (e.g. ^18.2.0). package-lock.json records the exact, deterministic tree of dependencies (including nested sub-dependencies and cryptographic integrity hashes) installed on your machine. This guarantees that every team member and production server installs the exact same bytes.",hi:"package.json dependencies ke approximate versions rakhta hai (jaise ^18.2.0). package-lock.json exact specific versions aur unke hash code lock karta hai taaki team ke sabhi computers aur production server par bilkul same version install ho."},takeaway:{en:"package.json is intent; package-lock.json is exact deterministic reality.",hi:"package-lock.json exact versions lock karta hai taaki bugs na aayein."}}]},{id:"summary",type:"summary",heading:{en:"Quick Summary",hi:"Quick Summary"},body:{en:"- Node.js LTS provides server runtime; npm manages open-source packages.\n- Git tracks history and allows branching.\n- Always include `.env` and `node_modules/` in `.gitignore`.\n- Use feature branches in professional team workflows.",hi:"- Node LTS server runtime deta hai aur npm packages manage karta hai.\n- Git history save karta hai aur checkpoints banata hai.\n- `.gitignore` mein hamesha `node_modules` aur `.env` zaroor rakhein.\n- Team mein kaam karte waqt feature branch use karein."}}],quiz:[{q:{en:"Why should you NOT commit the 'node_modules' folder to Git?",hi:"'node_modules' folder ko Git mein commit kyun nahi karna chahiye?"},options:[{en:"Because it contains copyrighted code that Git deletes automatically",hi:"Kyunki Git copyrighted code ko delete kar deta hai"},{en:"Because it contains thousands of heavy files that can be easily recreated by running 'npm install'",hi:"Kyunki isme hazaron heavy files hoti hain jo 'npm install' chalate hi dobara download ho jaati hain"},{en:"Because JavaScript fails to execute if uploaded to GitHub",hi:"Kyunki GitHub par upload hone par JS execute nahi hoti"},{en:"Because node_modules is only required in Python projects",hi:"Kyunki node_modules sirf Python projects mein use hoti hai"}],answerIndex:1,explanation:{en:"node_modules is huge (hundreds of MBs). Since package.json records all dependencies, any developer can simply run 'npm install' to recreate it in seconds.",hi:"node_modules bohot bada hota hai. Kyunki package.json mein saari list hoti hai, isliye koi bhi 'npm install' chalakar ise download kar sakta hai."}},{question:{en:"What is the core architectural purpose of Node.js, npm & Git Installation in the modern full-stack MERN ecosystem?",hi:"Modern full-stack MERN ecosystem mein Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide ka mukhya architectural maksad kya hota hai?"},options:[{en:"It manages physical computer cooling and power supply",hi:"Ye physical computer cooling aur power supply manage karta hai"},{en:"It provides structured, robust, and scalable patterns for handling node.js, npm & git installation with high performance and maintainability",hi:"Ye high performance aur maintainability ke saath Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide ko handle karne ka structured aur scalable pattern provide karta hai"},{en:"It completely replaces JavaScript with binary machine code in browser tabs",hi:"Ye browser tabs mein JavaScript ko binary machine code se replace karta hai"},{en:"It is only used for printing documents to physical printers",hi:"Ye sirf physical printers par documents print karne ke liye hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Node.js, npm & Git Installation establishes clean separation of concerns, ensuring predictable data flow, robust error handling, and optimal runtime performance in production.",hi:"Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide clean architecture aur separation of concerns deta hai jisse application scalable aur maintainable banti hai."}},{question:{en:"What critical development bottleneck or anti-pattern does Node.js, npm & Git Installation directly resolve?",hi:"Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide kis critical development bottleneck ya anti-pattern ko seedhe solve karta hai?"},options:[{en:"It replaces chaotic, tightly coupled ad-hoc logic with declarative, predictable control flow and structured data contracts",hi:"Ye chaotic aur tightly coupled logic ko hata kar declarative, predictable flow aur structured data contracts deta hai"},{en:"It forces the operating system to shut down when errors occur",hi:"Error aane par ye operating system band kar deta hai"},{en:"It deletes all database records older than 24 hours automatically",hi:"Ye 24 ghante purane DB records delete karta hai"},{en:"It blocks all outgoing HTTP network requests to conserve bandwidth",hi:"Ye bandwidth bachane ke liye network requests block karta hai"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Without Node.js, npm & Git Installation, applications suffer from brittle code, maintenance overhead, and unhandled edge cases that manifest as production crashes.",hi:"Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide ke bina code brittle ho jata hai aur production mein unexpected errors aate hain."}},{question:{en:"When reasoning about Node.js, npm & Git Installation, how is its mental model best conceptualized through real-world analogies?",hi:"Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide ko real-world analogies ke zariye kaise best samjha ja sakta hai?"},options:[{en:"As a completely offline computer with zero network or database connections",hi:"Ek offline computer ki tarah jisme koi connection na ho"},{en:"As a disciplined, coordinated workflow where inputs are validated and processed through standardized checkpoints rather than ad-hoc handling",hi:"Ek disciplined workflow ki tarah jahan data ko structured checkpoints ke zariye step-by-step process kiya jata hai"},{en:"As a random number generator with non-deterministic output",hi:"Random number generator ki tarah jiska koi niyam na ho"},{en:"As a static text document that cannot be modified or read",hi:"Static text document jo padha na ja sake"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Real-world workflow analogies help engineers visualize component boundaries, request lifecycles, and data transformations intuitively.",hi:"Real-world analogies component boundaries aur request lifecycle ko visual aur intuitive banati hain."}},{question:{en:"When declaring and implementing Node.js, npm & Git Installation, what syntactic convention is essential to prevent runtime errors?",hi:"Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide ko declare aur implement karte waqt kaunsa syntax niyam runtime errors rokne ke liye zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Adhering strictly to required parameters, handling asynchronous promises/callbacks cleanly, and verifying return value types",hi:"Zaroori parameters sahi pass karna, async promises ko handle karna aur return value types verify karna"},{en:"Wrapping every line of code inside an eval() execution block",hi:"Har line ko eval() block mein wrap karna"},{en:"Omitting import and require statements to reduce file size",hi:"File size ghatane ke liye import statements hatana"},{en:"Writing all code on a single continuous line without whitespace",hi:"Bina whitespace ke single line par code likhna"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Following standard ES6+ syntax contracts and properly handling promise resolution ensures execution safety and eliminates TypeError exceptions.",hi:"ES6+ syntax aur promise handling ke standard rules follow karne se TypeError aur crashes nahi aate."}},{question:{en:"What is a common pitfall developers encounter when working with Node.js, npm & Git Installation?",hi:"Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide ke saath kaam karte waqt developers aksar kaunsi aam galati karte hain?"},options:[{en:"Writing unit tests before implementing features",hi:"Feature likhne se pehle unit tests likhna"},{en:"Failing to handle failure edge cases, mutating shared state directly, or neglecting defensive validation guard clauses",hi:"Failure edge cases ko handle na karna, shared state direct mutate karna ya validation guard clauses na lagana"},{en:"Using strict equality checks (===) instead of loose equality (==)",hi:"Loose equality ke badle strict equality use karna"},{en:"Writing clear inline code documentation",hi:"Clear inline code comments likhna"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Neglecting edge cases and error handling causes silent regressions and race conditions that surface under concurrent user workloads.",hi:"Edge cases aur error handling miss karne se high-traffic production load mein silent bugs paida hote hain."}},{question:{en:"According to production best practices, how should Node.js, npm & Git Installation be architected for enterprise-grade stability?",hi:"Production best practices ke mutabiq enterprise-grade stability ke liye Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide ko kaise architect karna chahiye?"},options:[{en:"Enforce modular boundaries, validate all incoming payloads against schemas, log structured context, and maintain pure functions where possible",hi:"Modular boundaries enforce karein, payloads ko schema se validate karein, structured logs rakhein aur pure functions use karein"},{en:"Hardcode sensitive database connection strings directly in client-side files",hi:"Database passwords ko client files mein hardcode karna"},{en:"Disable all linter rules and type warnings globally",hi:"Linter aur type warnings ko globally disable karna"},{en:"Store all user session variables in global un-scoped memory arrays",hi:"Global memory arrays mein sessions store karna"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Enterprise-grade code prioritizes modularity, strict input validation, structured observability, and stateless designs.",hi:"Production hardening ke liye modular code, schema validation aur observability standard rules hote hain."}},{question:{en:"How does proper optimization of Node.js, npm & Git Installation impact application memory and CPU consumption?",hi:"Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide ko sahi dhang se optimize karne par application memory aur CPU par kya asar padta hai?"},options:[{en:"It increases server CPU temperature to 100 degrees Celsius",hi:"Server CPU temperature 100 degrees kar deta hai"},{en:"It minimizes redundant computations, eliminates memory leaks from uncleaned references, and maintains low latency under high concurrency",hi:"Ye redundant computations ghatata hai, memory leaks khatam karta hai aur high concurrency mein low latency maintain karta hai"},{en:"It doubles heap RAM allocation unconditionally",hi:"Heap RAM ko zabardasti double karta hai"},{en:"Optimization has zero measurable impact in modern web engines",hi:"Modern web engines par optimization ka koi asar nahi hota"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Preventing unnecessary allocations and cleaning up resources ensures low garbage collection pressure and predictable response times.",hi:"Memory leak rokne aur unnecessary allocations hatane se Garbage Collector par load kam rehta hai aur response fast rehta hai."}},{question:{en:"What security principle is non-negotiable when handling data within Node.js, npm & Git Installation?",hi:"Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide mein data handle karte waqt kaunsa security principle non-negotiable hota hai?"},options:[{en:"Never trust client-supplied input: always sanitize, authenticate, authorize, and validate against strict schemas on the server",hi:"Client data par blind trust na karein: server par hamesha sanitize, authenticate, authorize aur validate karein"},{en:"Trust all requests coming from mobile devices or web browsers blindly",hi:"Mobile ya browser se aane wali requests par blind trust karein"},{en:"Disable HTTPS and SSL certificates to maximize raw network throughput",hi:"Network throughput ke liye HTTPS band karein"},{en:"Expose database admin credentials to all registered users",hi:"Database admin credentials sabhi users ko expose karein"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Zero-Trust security dictates that every incoming request and data mutation must be validated and authenticated server-side before processing.",hi:"Zero-Trust security ke mutabiq har incoming mutation ko server par strictly validate aur authenticate kiya jana chahiye."}},{question:{en:"How does asynchronous non-blocking execution operate in Node.js, npm & Git Installation?",hi:"Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide mein asynchronous non-blocking execution kaise kaam karta hai?"},options:[{en:"It freezes the entire operating system until each operation completes",hi:"Har operation complete hone tak operating system freeze rehta hai"},{en:"I/O operations return Promises or accept callbacks, delegating work to background threads/queues while the main thread remains free to handle incoming tasks",hi:"I/O operations Promises return karte hain aur background queues use karke main thread ko baaki requests ke liye free rakhte hain"},{en:"Async operations execute in reverse alphabetical order automatically",hi:"Async operations reverse alphabetical order mein chalte hain"},{en:"Async code only executes when triggered manually by a user click",hi:"Sirf manual user click par async code chalta hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Non-blocking asynchronous operations resolve via microtasks or event loop queues, ensuring the runtime thread serves concurrent requests smoothly.",hi:"Non-blocking model main thread ko free rakhta hai taaki server bina rukaawat ke multiple users ko simultaneously serve kar sake."}},{question:{en:"What is the recommended pattern for propagating errors that occur in Node.js, npm & Git Installation?",hi:"Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide mein error aane par unhe propagate karne ka recommended pattern kya hai?"},options:[{en:"Intercepting the error, enriching it with operational context, and delegating to a centralized error handler or error boundary",hi:"Error ko intercept karna, debug context add karna, aur centralized error handler ya error boundary ko pass karna"},{en:"Swallowing errors silently with empty catch {} blocks to hide problems from logs",hi:"Khaali catch {} blocks se errors ko silently daba dena taaki logs mein na dikhein"},{en:"Shutting down the server machine power immediately",hi:"Server machine power turant band kar dena"},{en:"Sending internal raw stack traces and database credentials to end-user browsers",hi:"Raw stack trace aur DB passwords browser par bhej dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Centralized error propagation provides complete operational observability while shielding internal infrastructure details from end users.",hi:"Centralized error handling se system mein transparency rehti hai aur user ko clean, safe error messages milte hain."}},{question:{en:"When authoring unit or integration tests for Node.js, npm & Git Installation, what must the test suite assert?",hi:"Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide ke liye automated tests likhte waqt test suite ko kya assert karna zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Only that the JavaScript file can be saved to disk",hi:"Sirf ye ki file disk par save ho sake"},{en:"Both the happy path (expected inputs producing valid outputs) AND boundary edge cases (null, empty arrays, network timeouts, invalid types)",hi:"Happy path (valid data) AUR boundary edge cases (null, empty array, network timeout, invalid types) dono ko verify karna"},{en:"That the test suite takes at least 24 hours to finish running",hi:"Test suite ko 24 ghante chalna chahiye"},{en:"Testing is considered unnecessary in modern full-stack development",hi:"Modern development mein testing zaroori nahi hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Robust automated test suites verify both standard valid scenarios and defensive failure modes to prevent regressions during deployments.",hi:"Achhi testing valid inputs aur failure states dono ko assert karti hai taaki production deployments safe rahein."}},{question:{en:"How does modular design enhance code maintainability in Node.js, npm & Git Installation?",hi:"Modular design Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide mein code maintainability ko kaise badhata hai?"},options:[{en:"By isolating distinct responsibilities into small, reusable, and independently testable units following the Single Responsibility Principle",hi:"Single Responsibility Principle ke zariye alag-alag kaamo ko chote, reusable aur testable units mein baant kar"},{en:"By combining all frontend, backend, and database code into a single 50,000-line script",hi:"Saara code ek hi 50,000-line script mein daal kar"},{en:"By removing all function names and replacing them with random numbers",hi:"Function names hata kar random numbers likhna"},{en:"By forbidding code comments and documentation across the repository",hi:"Comments aur documentation ban kar dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Modularity reduces cognitive load, simplifies debugging, prevents ripple effects during changes, and enables seamless team collaboration.",hi:"Modular code se readability badhti hai, debugging aasan hoti hai aur ek jagah badlav karne par doosri jagah bugs nahi aate."}},{question:{en:"When application traffic scales 100x, how should Node.js, npm & Git Installation be architected to support horizontal scaling?",hi:"Traffic 100x badhne par Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide ko horizontally scale karne ke liye kya design approach honi chahiye?"},options:[{en:"Ensure the component/service is completely stateless, offload shared session/state to Redis/MongoDB, and distribute traffic via a load balancer",hi:"Service ko completely stateless banayein, shared state ko Redis/DB par shift karein aur load balancer se traffic distribute karein"},{en:"Store all user session variables in local in-memory JavaScript objects on the web server",hi:"Server ki local RAM mein session variables store karna"},{en:"Reboot the production server manually whenever memory usage exceeds 10%",hi:"Memory 10% cross hote hi server manually reboot karna"},{en:"Block 95% of incoming users using firewall rules",hi:"95% users ko firewall se block kar dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Stateless service architecture guarantees that any container instance can handle any incoming request, enabling dynamic auto-scaling without session loss.",hi:"Stateless architecture auto-scaling ka base hai jahan naye containers bina session loss ke instant traffic handle kar sakte hain."}},{question:{en:"In the full-stack MERN paradigm, where does Node.js, npm & Git Installation properly belong and execute?",hi:"Full-stack MERN architecture mein Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide kahan belong karta hai aur kahan execute hota hai?"},options:[{en:"In its designated architectural tier (Client browser UI, Express API backend, or MongoDB database) with clean API contracts connecting them",hi:"Apne designated tier (Browser UI, Express API backend, ya MongoDB) mein clean API contracts ke saath"},{en:"Directly on the end-user's local router firmware",hi:"User ke local router firmware par"},{en:"Inside the computer motherboard BIOS chip",hi:"Motherboard BIOS chip mein"},{en:"All MERN code runs strictly inside the MongoDB database engine",hi:"Saara MERN code sirf MongoDB ke andar chalta hai"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Maintaining clear structural boundaries between client rendering, backend orchestration, and database persistence is the defining trait of MERN.",hi:"Client UI, backend server aur database ke beech saaf boundary maintain karna MERN architecture ka mukhya niyam hai."}},{question:{en:"What telemetry metric or observability signal is most crucial for diagnosing issues with Node.js, npm & Git Installation in production?",hi:"Production mein Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide ki problems diagnose karne ke liye sabse zaroori telemetry metric kaunsi hoti hai?"},options:[{en:"The desktop monitor brightness setting of the client",hi:"Client ke monitor ki brightness"},{en:"Latency percentiles (p95/p99), error rates (HTTP 4xx/5xx), throughput (RPS), and heap memory allocation deltas",hi:"Latency percentiles (p95/p99), error rates (4xx/5xx), throughput (RPS), aur heap memory allocation deltas"},{en:"The number of files in the project's root folder",hi:"Root folder mein files ki sankhya"},{en:"The physical keyboard model used by the engineer",hi:"Engineer ke keyboard ka model"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Observability platforms monitor p95/p99 latencies, error frequencies, and memory utilization to identify bottlenecks and regressions early.",hi:"p95/p99 latencies aur error rates monitor karne se crashes aane se pehle hi bottlenecks pakad mein aa jaate hain."}},{question:{en:"Why is eliminating unintended side effects essential when authoring logic for Node.js, npm & Git Installation?",hi:"Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide ka logic likhte waqt unintended side effects ko khatam karna kyun zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Side effects introduce unpredictability, corrupt shared state, cause race conditions, and make concurrent code nearly impossible to debug",hi:"Side effects se code unpredictable banta hai, shared state corrupt hoti hai aur race conditions create hoti hain"},{en:"Side effects permanently erase the developer's Git commit history",hi:"Git history permanently delete ho jaati hai"},{en:"Side effects are strictly required by the JavaScript ECMAScript standard",hi:"ECMAScript mein side effects required hain"},{en:"Side effects make all algorithms execute in O(1) time",hi:"Saare algorithms O(1) time mein chalte hain"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Pure and predictable logic produces the same output for identical inputs, guaranteeing thread safety, easy caching, and high reliability.",hi:"Pure logic se shared state safe rehti hai aur same input par hamesha consistent aur predictable output milta hai."}},{question:{en:"How should client-side state be kept in sync with backend server mutations in Node.js, npm & Git Installation?",hi:"Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide mein client-side state aur backend server data ko sync mein kaise rakha jata hai?"},options:[{en:"By forcing a complete hard page refresh every 3 seconds",hi:"Har 3 second mein poora page hard refresh karke"},{en:"Using optimistic UI updates with error rollback, automated query cache invalidation (TanStack Query/RTK), or WebSocket change streams",hi:"Optimistic UI updates with rollback, automated query cache invalidation ya WebSocket push streams use karke"},{en:"By disabling all database update operations permanently",hi:"Database updates ko permanently band karke"},{en:"By saving user state in local CSV files on the server desktop",hi:"Server desktop par CSV files save karke"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Modern full-stack architectures synchronize state seamlessly using query cache invalidation, optimistic updates, and real-time socket events.",hi:"Modern apps cache invalidation aur optimistic UI use karti hain taaki UI bina screen reload ke instantly updated rahe."}},{question:{en:"Why is thorough resource cleanup (clearing timers, closing sockets, aborting in-flight requests) critical in Node.js, npm & Git Installation?",hi:"Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide mein resource cleanup (timers clear karna, sockets band karna, network abort karna) kyun zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"To prevent memory leaks where unreachable or orphaned objects remain retained in heap memory, causing gradual performance degradation and crashes",hi:"Memory leaks rokne ke liye taaki unneeded objects RAM mein jama na hon aur server crash na ho"},{en:"To delete the client's local disk partition",hi:"Client ka local disk partition delete karne ke liye"},{en:"Because JavaScript engines allow only 5 variables in RAM",hi:"JS engine sirf 5 variables allow karta hai"},{en:"Cleanup is unnecessary because garbage collection handles 100% of event listeners automatically",hi:"Cleanup ki zaroorat nahi hoti"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Unclosed connections and dangling event listeners create references that prevent garbage collection, leading to severe memory leaks over time.",hi:"Dangling listeners aur unclosed connections memory leaks banate hain jo V8 heap ko exhaust karke process crash kar dete hain."}},{question:{en:"What principle enables Node.js, npm & Git Installation to operate identically across local dev, staging, and production environments?",hi:"Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide ko local dev, staging aur production mein bilkul same operate karne ke liye kaunsa niyam zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Twelve-Factor App methodology: injecting all environment-specific configurations and credentials via environment variables rather than hardcoded code",hi:"Twelve-Factor niyam: environment variables se dynamic configuration aur credentials inject karna bina code badle"},{en:"Manually rewriting the codebase before deploying to each server",hi:"Har server par deploy karne se pehle naya code likhna"},{en:"Hosting development and production on the same physical developer laptop",hi:"Ek hi laptop par dev aur prod dono host karna"},{en:"Disabling all security authentications in production environments",hi:"Production mein saari security band kar dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Decoupling configuration from executable code allows identical, immutable container images to run reliably across all deployment stages.",hi:"Config aur code ko alag rakhne se ek hi build image bina kisi bug ke kisi bhi cloud platform par chal sakti hai."}},{question:{en:"When an unexpected outage or regression occurs in production involving Node.js, npm & Git Installation, what is the first engineering step?",hi:"Production mein Node.js, npm & Git Installation Guide se related outage ya regression aane par pehla engineering step kya hona chahiye?"},options:[{en:"Immediately delete all production databases without backups",hi:"Bina backup ke production database delete kar dena"},{en:"Check centralized observability logs and error stack traces, correlate request IDs, reproduce locally with minimal test cases, and isolate the root cause",hi:"Centralized observability logs aur stack traces check karna, request ID correlate karna, aur locally minimal test cases se reproduce karna"},{en:"Blame the operating system without inspecting any server logs",hi:"Bina log dekhe OS ko blame karna"},{en:"Wait several days hoping the system resolves itself",hi:"Kai din intezar karna"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Disciplined engineering incident response begins with analyzing structured logs, tracing request flow, and isolating reproducible root causes.",hi:"Disciplined debugging structured logs aur request correlation ID dekh kar root cause isolate karne se shuru hoti hai."}}]};export{e as default};
